page ErrorT11(path: "/errors/T11", title: "T11 — A match on something that cannot be matched", description: "A `match` is over a resource (`loading`, `error`, `ready`) or an enum (`.case`); its arms are of that kind.") {
    ErrorShell("T11", title: "A match on something that cannot be matched", severity: "error", family: "Types", summary: "A `match` is over a resource (`loading`, `error`, `ready`) or an enum (`.case`); its arms are of that kind.", printed: #"error[T11]: `match` needs a resource or an enum, but `n` is `Number`
 --> src/App.wf:4:5
  |
4 |     match n {
  |     ^^^^^^^^^
  = help: Use `if` for a condition; `match` chooses among a resource's states or an enum's cases
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/T11"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: false, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/T11.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state n = 1
    Heading("Match").h1
    match n {
        loading { Spinner }
        else { Text("?") }
    }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state n = 1
    Heading("Match").h1
    if n == 1 { Text("One") } else { Text("?") }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Use `if` for a condition; `match` takes a resource, a connection or an enum.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorT12(path: "/errors/T12", title: "T12 — A secret where it would escape", description: "A `Secret` shown by an element, spliced into text, logged or kept with `persist`.") {
    ErrorShell("T12", title: "A secret where it would escape", severity: "error", family: "Types", summary: "A `Secret` shown by an element, spliced into text, logged or kept with `persist`.", printed: #"error[T12]: `token` is a `Secret`, and `Text` would show it
 --> src/App.wf:4:10
  |
4 |     Text(token)
  |          ^^^^^
  = help: A secret must not reach the page; send it as a value, or show one field of what it unlocks
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/T12"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: false, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/T12.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state token: Secret = ""
    Heading("Token").h1
    Text(token)
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state token: Secret = ""
    Heading("Token").h1
    Button("Sign in") { on click { fetch("/api/session", method: "POST", body: { token: token }) } }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Do not show, splice, log or persist a `Secret`. Send it in a request — or keep it on the server.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorT13(path: "/errors/T13", title: "T13 — A name nothing declares", description: "A name, or a function called, that no declaration, parameter, script or browser global provides — a ReferenceError the first time the page reads it.") {
    ErrorShell("T13", title: "A name nothing declares", severity: "error", family: "Types", summary: "A name, or a function called, that no declaration, parameter, script or browser global provides — a ReferenceError the first time the page reads it.", printed: #"error[T13]: nothing declares `cuont`
 --> src/App.wf:4:30
  |
4 |     Button("+") { on click { cuont = count + 1 } }
  |                              ^^^^^
  = help: Did you mean `count`? Declare it — a `state`, a `const`, an `action`, a prop — or check the spelling. In the browser it would be a ReferenceError
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/T13"#, quickfix: "Change to `count`", lowerable: false, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/T13.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state count = 0
    Heading("Counter").h1
    Button("+") { on click { cuont = count + 1 } }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state count = 0
    Heading("Counter").h1
    Button("+") { on click { count = count + 1 } }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Correct the spelling, or declare the name. The browser's own\nglobals (`window`, `navigator`, `Math` …) and the language's values\n(`viewport`, `query`, `now` …) need no declaration; a call to a function\nnothing declares — `uid()` for `uuid()` — is reported the same way. A\ntemplate rendered with data (`wf render`) reads its data's keys by name, so\nit is not held to this.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorT16(path: "/errors/T16", title: "T16 — A method a number, a string or a list does not have", description: "In the browser the call is `x.method is not a function`, the first time the line runs. The message suggests the nearest method there is.") {
