}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state count = 0
    Heading("Count").h1
    if count == 0 { Text("Nothing yet") }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Compare values of one type: `count == 0`, or convert one side\n(`Number(text) == n`). Against an enum, use a case it has.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorT17(path: "/errors/T17", title: "T17 — An async result used before it is awaited", description: "An action that awaits hands back a promise; read as its result without `await` it is not one. `await` is written in an action, a handler, a timer or…") {
    ErrorShell("T17", title: "An async result used before it is awaited", severity: "error", family: "Types", summary: "An action that awaits hands back a promise; read as its result without `await` it is not one. `await` is written in an action, a handler, a timer or a hook — not in a `derived` value or an effect, which run at once — and `.pending` is for an action that awaits.", printed: #"error[T17]: `save` awaits nothing, so `.pending` is always false
 --> src/App.wf:5:30
  |
5 |     Button("Save", disabled: save.pending) { on click { save() } }
  |                              ^^^^
  = help: `.pending` is true while a call of an async action runs; an action that awaits nothing finishes before the page repaints
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/T17"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: false, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/T17.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state saved = false
    action save() { saved = true }
    Heading("Save").h1
    Button("Save", disabled: save.pending) { on click { save() } }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state saved = false
    action save() { saved = true }
    Heading("Save").h1
    Button("Save", disabled: saved) { on click { save() } }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("`.pending` is for an action that awaits — drop it here. An async\naction's result is read with `await` inside an action or a handler; a value\nthat arrives over the network is a `resource`, which `derived` values and\nelements can read.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorT19(path: "/errors/T19", title: "T19 — A value that may be null, shown as text", description: "Spliced into text, `null` shows as `null` (and a missing value as `undefined`). Say what to show instead with `??`.") {
    ErrorShell("T19", title: "A value that may be null, shown as text", severity: "warning", family: "Types", summary: "Spliced into text, `null` shows as `null` (and a missing value as `undefined`). Say what to show instead with `??`.", printed: #"warning[T19]: `user.nickname` may be null, and in text it would show as `null`
