page ErrorT18(path: "/errors/T18", title: "T18 — Arithmetic on something that is not a number", description: "`-`, `*`, `/` and `%` take numbers; on a string or a list the result is `NaN`. `+` joins text when one side is a string, and takes numbers otherwise.") {
    ErrorShell("T18", title: "Arithmetic on something that is not a number", severity: "error", family: "Types", summary: "`-`, `*`, `/` and `%` take numbers; on a string or a list the result is `NaN`. `+` joins text when one side is a string, and takes numbers otherwise.", printed: #"error[T18]: `*` takes numbers, but `price` is `String`
 --> src/App.wf:3:27
  |
3 |     Heading("Total {price * 2}").h1
  |                           ^
  = help: Convert it: `Number(value)`; `+` joins text when one side is a string
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/T18"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: false, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/T18.md") {
