page ErrorC07(path: "/errors/C07", title: "C07 — A drag or a gesture on a component with no one element", description: "`drag:`, `dragGroup:`, `dropValue:`, `dropAxis:`, `dropInside:`, `on receive(d)`, `on dragmove(d)`, `on longpress` and `on swipe` written on your…") {
    ErrorShell("C07", title: "A drag or a gesture on a component with no one element", severity: "error", family: "Components", summary: "`drag:`, `dragGroup:`, `dropValue:`, `dropAxis:`, `dropInside:`, `on receive(d)`, `on dragmove(d)`, `on longpress` and `on swipe` written on your component's call belong to the one element it draws. A component whose body is an `if`, a `for`, a `show`, a `match` or several elements has none to give them, so wrap what it draws in one element, or write them inside it.", printed: #"error[C07]: `drag:` on `Rows2` has no element to land on: its body is a `for`
 --> src/App.wf:6:16
  |
6 |     Rows2("a", drag: "a")
  |                ^^^^
  = help: Wrap what `Rows2` draws in one element (a `Stack`, a `Row`), or write `drag:` inside it
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/C07"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: false, why: true, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix")), Anchor(id: "why", label: t("error.why"))], source: "md-docs/errors/C07.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"component Rows2(_ name: String) {
    for x in [1, 2] { Text(name) }
}
page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Files").h1
    Rows2("a", drag: "a")
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"component Rows2(_ name: String) {
    Stack { for x in [1, 2] { Text(name) } }
}
page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Files").h1
    Rows2("a", drag: "a")
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Wrap what the component draws in one element — a `Stack`, a `Row`\n— or write the drag inside it, on the element it is for.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
        Markdown("`drag:`, `dragGroup:`, `dropValue:`, `dropAxis:`, `dropInside:` and the\nhandlers of the gestures — `on receive(d)`, `on dragmove(d)`, `on\nlongpress`, `on swipe` — written on your component's call belong to the one\nelement it draws. A body that is an `if`, a `for`, a `show`, a `match` or\nseveral elements has no one element to give them.")
    }
}

page ErrorR01(path: "/errors/R01", title: "R01 — A route to nothing", description: "A link, a `navigate()` or a `Route` names a page or a path that no page has.") {
    ErrorShell("R01", title: "A route to nothing", severity: "error", family: "Routes", summary: "A link, a `navigate()` or a `Route` names a page or a path that no page has.", printed: #"error[R01]: `/abuot` is not a route: no page's `path` matches it
 --> src/App.wf:3:5
  |
3 |     Link("About us", to: "/abuot")
  |     ^^^^
  = help: The nearest is `/about`
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/R01"#, quickfix: "Change to `/about`", lowerable: true, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/R01.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page Home(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Home").h1
    Link("About us", to: "/abuot")
}
page About(path: "/about", title: "About", description: "D") {
    Heading("About").h1
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page Home(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Home").h1
    Link("About us", to: "/about")
}
page About(path: "/about", title: "About", description: "D") {
    Heading("About").h1
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Link to a route a page has; the message names the nearest. A\nspliced link is checked by its shape — `\"/team/\{t.slug\}\"` must match a route\nlike `/team/:slug` — a link with no leading `/` is refused (where it leads\nwould depend on the page it is on), and a link to a file (`/report.pdf`) or\nanother site is left alone.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorR02(path: "/errors/R02", title: "R02 — A route parameter and a page parameter that do not match", description: "A route's `:name` fills the page's parameter of that name; a `:name` with no parameter is read as nothing, and a parameter with no `:name` is never filled.") {
    ErrorShell("R02", title: "A route parameter and a page parameter that do not match", severity: "error", family: "Routes", summary: "A route's `:name` fills the page's parameter of that name; a `:name` with no parameter is read as nothing, and a parameter with no `:name` is never filled.", printed: #"error[R02]: the route `/u/:id` names `:id`, and the page declares no parameter `id`
 --> src/App.wf:1:1
  |
1 | page Profile(path: "/u/:id", title: "T", description: "D") {
  | ^^^^
  = help: Declare it: `page Profile(path: "/u/:id", id: String)`, then read `id`
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/R02"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: false, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/R02.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page Profile(path: "/u/:id", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Profile").h1
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page Profile(path: "/u/:id", title: "T", description: "D", id: String) {
    Heading("Profile {id}").h1
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Declare the parameter the route names — `page Profile(path:\n\"/u/:id\", id: String)` — and read it by name; a declared parameter the route\nhas no `:name` for is never filled.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorR03(path: "/errors/R03", title: "R03 — An app with no Router, or with two", description: "The current page is drawn where `app` places its `Router`. With none, no page is ever drawn; with two, the page has two places.") {
    ErrorShell("R03", title: "An app with no Router, or with two", severity: "error", family: "Routes", summary: "The current page is drawn where `app` places its `Router`. With none, no page is ever drawn; with two, the page has two places.", printed: #"error[R03]: `app` places no `Router`, so no page is ever drawn
 --> src/App.wf:2:5
