page ErrorV01(path: "/errors/V01", title: "V01 — A bare word that means nothing", description: "A bare word in an argument that nothing in scope declares — a misspelled name, or a flag written without its dot.") {
    ErrorShell("V01", title: "A bare word that means nothing", severity: "warning", family: "Vocabulary", summary: "A bare word in an argument that nothing in scope declares — a misspelled name, or a flag written without its dot.", printed: #"warning[V01]: nothing in scope declares `primary`, so it reads as nothing — a flag is written `.primary`
 --> src/App.wf:3:12
  |
3 |     Button(primary)
  |            ^^^^^^^
  = help: did you mean `.primary`?
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/V01"#, quickfix: "Write it as the flag `.primary`", lowerable: true, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [RelatedLink(kind: "T13", title: "A name nothing declares", to: "/errors/T13")], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/V01.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Save").h1
    Button(primary)
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Save").h1
    Button("Save").primary
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Write the flag with its dot — `Button(\"Save\").primary` — or declare the name. The word is also a name nothing declares, so the build stops on it as `T13`; the editor shows both.\n\nA name a branch binds is declared through the whole of its block, however\ndeep the element that reads it: `if let why = e.reason \{ Row \{ Pill(why) \} \}`,\nand a case's payload, `.failed(why) \{ … \}`, draw nothing.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorV02(path: "/errors/V02", title: "V02 — A flag no stylesheet styles", description: "A flag whose class no stylesheet — the engine's or one of the project's — defines.") {
    ErrorShell("V02", title: "A flag no stylesheet styles", severity: "warning", family: "Vocabulary", summary: "A flag whose class no stylesheet — the engine's or one of the project's — defines.", printed: #""#, quickfix: "", lowerable: true, why: true, example: false, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix")), Anchor(id: "why", label: t("error.why"))], source: "md-docs/errors/V02.md") {
        fixed {
            Stack(gap: .sm) {
                Markdown("define the class in a `.css`\nfile under `src/`, or drop the flag.")
            }
        }
        Markdown("A flag on one of your components whose class no stylesheet — the engine's\nor one of the project's `.css` files — defines, so it changes nothing on\nscreen. The built-ins cannot draw it: the registry and the engine's\nstylesheet are held to each other.")
    }
}

page ErrorV03(path: "/errors/V03", title: "V03 — Markup put in as markup", description: "An `Unsafe.Html`, and whether what it puts in went through `sanitize`; and a `Frame(srcdoc:)` drawing HTML from a value, which is sandboxed…") {
    ErrorShell("V03", title: "Markup put in as markup", severity: "warning", family: "Vocabulary", summary: "An `Unsafe.Html`, and whether what it puts in went through `sanitize`; and a `Frame(srcdoc:)` drawing HTML from a value, which is sandboxed (`sandbox=\"\"`) unless it says what it may do.", printed: #"warning[V03]: `Unsafe.Html` puts markup in as markup
 --> src/App.wf:4:5
  |
4 |     Unsafe.Html(body)
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: Anything the project did not write itself belongs in `sanitize(…)` first
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/V03"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: true, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/V03.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state body = "<b>Hi</b>"
    Heading("Markup").h1
    Unsafe.Html(body)
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    state body = "**Hi**"
    Heading("Markup").h1
    Markdown(body)
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Most text wants no markup of its own: write it as Markdown,\nwhich `Markdown(body)` draws with any HTML in it shown as text. Markup that\nmust stay markup and comes from outside the project goes through\n`sanitize(…)` first — `Unsafe.Html(sanitize(body))` — which is the reviewed\ncase, and the warning still names it.\n\nA `Frame(srcdoc:)` drawing HTML from a value is named too: that HTML is\na document of its own, scripts and all. Unless the call says what the\nframe may do, it may do nothing — the build gives it `sandbox=\"\"` —\nand the warning says so. Writing `sandbox:` out is the reviewed case;\n`allow-scripts` with `allow-same-origin` undoes the sandbox, and is\nnamed again.\n\n```wf expect=V03\npage P(path: \"/\", title: \"T\", description: \"D\") \{\n    state html = \"<p>Hi</p>\"\n    Heading(\"Preview\").h1\n    Frame(srcdoc: html, title: \"Preview\")\n\}\n```\n\n```text\nwarning[V03]: `Frame(srcdoc:)` draws HTML from a value as a document; it is sandboxed (`sandbox=\"\"`), so nothing in it runs\n --> src/App.wf:4:5\n  |\n4 |     Frame(srcdoc: html, title: \"Preview\")\n  |     ^^^^^\n  = help: Say what it may do with `sandbox:` — `sandbox: \"\"` keeps it as it is now; `allow-scripts` and `allow-same-origin` together undo the sandbox\n  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/V03\n```\n\n**Fix:** `Frame(srcdoc: html, title: \"Preview\", sandbox: \"\")`.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorV04(path: "/errors/V04", title: "V04 — A class that is the engine's", description: "A `class:` naming one of the built-ins' `wf-*` classes, which brings that built-in's rules with it.") {
    ErrorShell("V04", title: "A class that is the engine's", severity: "warning", family: "Vocabulary", summary: "A `class:` naming one of the built-ins' `wf-*` classes, which brings that built-in's rules with it.", printed: #"warning[V04]: `class:` names `wf-btn`, one of the engine's own classes
 --> src/App.wf:3:5
  |
3 |     Card(class: "wf-btn") { Text("x") }
  |     ^^^^
  = help: `wf-` classes are the built-ins': one added here brings another built-in's rules with it. Name a class of your own, or use the flag that sets the look
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/V04"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: true, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/V04.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Classes").h1
    Card(class: "wf-btn") { Text("x") }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Classes").h1
    Card(class: "note") { Text("x") }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("Name a class of your own and style it in a `.css` file under `src/`, or use the flag that sets the look you wanted (`.primary`, `.elevated`).")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorV05(path: "/errors/V05", title: "V05 — A CSS property no browser knows", description: "A misspelled property — `colr:` — is ignored by the browser; nothing tells you why the style did not take.") {
    ErrorShell("V05", title: "A CSS property no browser knows", severity: "warning", family: "Vocabulary", summary: "A misspelled property — `colr:` — is ignored by the browser; nothing tells you why the style did not take.", printed: #"warning[V05]: `colr` is not a CSS property, so the browser ignores it
 --> src/App.wf:3:17
  |
3 |         style { colr: red }
  |                 ^^^^
  = help: Did you mean `color`?
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/V05"#, quickfix: "Change to `color`", lowerable: true, why: true, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix")), Anchor(id: "why", label: t("error.why"))], source: "md-docs/errors/V05.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Hello") {
        style { colr: red }
    }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Hello").h1 {
        style { color: red }
    }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("The property the message suggests — here `color`. A custom\nproperty is written `--name`.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
        Markdown("Warning.")
    }
}

page ErrorV06(path: "/errors/V06", title: "V06 — A design token the theme does not declare", description: "`$name` compiles to `var(--name)`; a token the theme does not declare is never set, so the property falls back to nothing.") {
    ErrorShell("V06", title: "A design token the theme does not declare", severity: "error", family: "Vocabulary", summary: "`$name` compiles to `var(--name)`; a token the theme does not declare is never set, so the property falls back to nothing.", printed: #"error[V06]: `$brnad` is no token the theme declares, so it is never set
 --> src/App.wf:3:17
  |
3 |         style { color: $brnad }
  |                 ^^^^^
  = help: Declare it in your `theme { … }`, or use one the theme has
  = docs: https://webfluent.monzeromer.dev/errors/V06"#, quickfix: "", lowerable: false, why: false, example: true, families: ERROR_INDEX, related: [], sections: [Anchor(id: "printed", label: t("error.printed")), Anchor(id: "fix", label: t("error.fix"))], source: "md-docs/errors/V06.md") {
        broken { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Hello") {
        style { color: $brnad }
    }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        fixed { CodeBlock(#"page P(path: "/", title: "T", description: "D") {
    Heading("Hello").h1 {
        style { color: $color-primary }
    }
}"#, title: "wf") }
        note {
            Markdown("A token the theme has — a short name resolves through the\nproperty (`padding: $lg`, `border: 1px solid $border`) — or declare it in\nyour `theme \{ … \}`.")
            Markdown("Each example is a whole program: it is all of `src/App.wf` in a project with no other `.wf` file ([trying an example](/errors#trying-an-example)).") { style { font-size: 14px; color: $muted } }
        }
    }
}

page ErrorV07(path: "/errors/V07", title: "V07 — A number where CSS wants a length", description: "`width: \{pct\}` with a number is a length with no unit, which the browser drops. Give it one: `\{pct\}%`.") {
    ErrorShell("V07", title: "A number where CSS wants a length", severity: "warning", family: "Vocabulary", summary: "`width: \{pct\}` with a number is a length with no unit, which the browser drops. Give it one: `\{pct\}%`.", printed: #"warning[V07]: `width: {pct}` is a number with no unit, which the browser drops
 --> src/App.wf:4:20
